 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for committed changes.** Low-latency updates without a realtime provider justify operating connection capacity and reconnects. Five-second HTTPS polling offers simpler stateless operation but adds repeated reads and delivery lag; a hosted realtime service reduces connection operations but introduces recurring fees and provider coupling. See [Delivery of Committed Board Changes](decisions/change-delivery.md).
